 all three films were number one  on netflix it was unbelievable i'm  having a great year you know i'm pretty  much  you've said that your stories are a  combination of humor and fear why has  that always been a good combination for  you why do you like to add humor to that  you know the secret is i the secret is i  never um  i never planned to be scary  i never wanted that wasn't my goal i  always was funny  i did a humor magazine for 10 teenagers  for 10 years called bananas and i wrote  about 100 joke books  i'm always funny  and so when i  got switched over which is sort of a  long story and started being a scary guy  i brought i had to bring the humor with  me because that's my main interest  really  you've said too that the scary stuff  doesn't scare you so when did you  realize that i mean was it reading scary  books was it watching scary movies and  not having the same reaction that other  people have those people coming to me  and saying after i read your book i had  to leave all the lights on and i locked  all the doors and i and i thought gee  i've never had that feeling from  anything  i've never had it it's just something  missing in me i think  what were the stories that most inspired  you as a kid what did what do you think  had the biggest influence on your  writing  um  well a lot of things i think a lot but  um when i was a kid there were these  scary comic books these horror comics  called tales from the crypt and the  vault of horror and they were very very  influential on me they were  gory gruesome  horror stories with brilliant art and  they all had a funny twist ending every  story had a funny twist at the end and  it's sort of that sort of it's what i  try to do  do you have other adaptations that are  currently in development or in the works  now do you know like what the next thing  based on your work could be  um  well i don't know if i can talk about  them  i don't know there's a you know i did  these four books um  y.a books called the 